# Written by `python -m harness init`. Covers what the harness itself writes,
# and nothing else — you almost certainly want to add your language's rules
# (__pycache__/, node_modules/, .venv/) on top. A file that tried to be a
# complete .gitignore for every project would be incomplete for all of them.
#
# The one rule underneath all of this: provenance is committed, bytes are not.
# A manifest says what was tried and what won, and it is small. The artifact it
# describes is not, and `promote()` copies your model into champion/, so the
# same bytes land in two places on every promotion. A run history of any length
# then becomes a repository nobody can clone — and by the time that is
# noticeable, the bytes are in the history and hard to get out.

runs/*/artifacts/
runs/*/checkpoints/
champion/*.onnx
champion/*.mlpackage/
champion/*.tflite
champion/*.safetensors
data/
corpora/
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.gguf

# These ARE tracked. They are the decision trail: what ran, what it scored,
# and what became the champion. Nothing above matches them — the negations are
# here to say so, not because they are load-bearing. Do not "tidy" this by
# ignoring runs/ or champion/ wholesale.
!runs/*/manifest.json
!runs/LEDGER.md
!champion/champion.json
